❯ Can you explain how rate_source works at a high level

⏺ rate_source is an injectable callable — meaning you pass it into Desk at
  construction time, and the desk calls it internally.

  It has the signature rate_source(pair: str) -> int and returns the mid-rate
  for a currency pair in basis points, where 10,000 bps = 1.0000. So
  rate_source("EURUSD") might return 10842, meaning 1 EUR = 1.0842 USD.

  The desk only calls it once — at close() time — to lock in rates for all
  submitted pairs at that moment.

